      ],
      "observed": "Every VDD pin on both MCU symbols is shown on an unconnected net; none is connected to a supply rail.",
      "expected": "Both MCUs' VDD pins must be powered from the regulated 3.3 V rail. The specification says 3.3 V feeds both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"11\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"19\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As represented, neither MCU receives its core supply, so the flight-control and navigation computers cannot operate.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["FCC2", "UART3_FCC2", "C60"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.48", "FCC2.73", "UART3_FCC2.3", "UART3_FCC2.4", "C60.1"],
      "nets": ["NET0002", "NET0014", "unconnected-(C60-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC MCU's two VCAP pins are routed to pins 3 and 4 of UART3_FCC2, rather than to VCAP capacitors; C60 pin 1 is unconnected.",
      "expected": "The STM32H753 VCAP pins should have their required local capacitors to ground and should not be used as UART connector signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0002\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0014\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"unconnected-(C60-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C60\") (pin \"1\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The H753's required internal-regulator bypassing is absent, and the UART connector exposes the VCAP nets; the FCC may fail to start or operate unreliably.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["REG1"],
      "pins": ["REG1.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The regulator output is on +3.3V, while +3V3 is a separate net with no connection to REG1. The netlist therefore represents two isolated 3.3 V nets.",
      "expected": "The board's single regulated 3.3 V rail should supply the circuitry and distribution points assigned to that rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Loads connected only to +3V3 are not connected to the LDO output and may be left unpowered.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs' VDD pins are unconnected, and the FCC's VCAP pins are routed to UART connector pins instead of bypass capacitors. The netlist also shows the regulated +3.3V rail isolated from +3V3."
}

